# Metadata Section

## Purpose

Defines the Metadata section of the MAM specification. The YAML front matter carries machine readable identity for the module including id, version, name, author, runtime, tags, and license.

## Inputs

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| content | string | Yes | Full MAM module text with front matter |
| metadata | object | No | Metadata object to validate directly |

## Outputs

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| metadata | object | Parsed front matter data |
| valid | bool | Whether the metadata passes validation |
| errors | list | Validation errors found in the metadata |

## Capabilities

### validate

Checks required fields, id format, version format, and runtime values.

### extract

Pulls the front matter out of the module text.

### document

Renders the metadata into a documentation fragment.

## Rules

- Every module must declare id, version, name, author, and runtime.
- The id must be lowercase with letters, digits, and single hyphens.
- The version must follow semantic versioning.
- The name is the human readable module name.
- The runtime must be one of the supported languages.
- Optional fields enrich discovery and tooling.

## Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Content] --> B[Extract]
    B --> C[Validate]
    C --> D[Document]
    D --> E[Output]
```

## Python

```python
import re

def validate_id(id_value: str) -> bool:
    return bool(re.match(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$", id_value))

def validate_version(version: str) -> bool:
    return bool(re.match(r"^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+", version))

def validate_runtime(runtime: str) -> bool:
    return runtime in ("python", "javascript", "typescript", "rust", "go", "shell", "mixed")

def validate_required(metadata: dict) -> list:
    required = ["id", "version", "name", "author", "runtime"]
    missing = []
    for field in required:
        if field not in metadata:
            missing.append(field)
    return missing

def extract_metadata(content: str) -> dict:
    if not content.startswith("---"):
        return {}
    end = content.find("---", 3)
    if end == -1:
        return {}
    metadata = {}
    for line in content[3:end].split("\n"):
        if ":" in line and not line.strip().startswith("-"):
            key, value = line.split(":", 1)
            metadata[key.strip()] = value.strip().strip("\"'")
    return metadata

def validate_metadata(metadata: dict) -> list:
    errors = []
    for field in validate_required(metadata):
        errors.append("Missing required field: " + field)
    if "id" in metadata and not validate_id(metadata["id"]):
        errors.append("Invalid id: " + str(metadata["id"]))
    if "version" in metadata and not validate_version(str(metadata["version"])):
        errors.append("Invalid version: " + str(metadata["version"]))
    return errors

def document_metadata(metadata: dict) -> str:
    docs = "# Module Metadata\n\n"
    for key, value in metadata.items():
        docs += "- " + key + ": " + str(value) + "\n"
    return docs
```

## Tests

### Input

```yaml
content: |
  ---
  id: user-auth
  name: User Auth
  version: 1.0.0
  author: MAM Team
  runtime: python
  ---
```

### Expected

```yaml
valid: true
errors: []
```

```python
def test_metadata():
    content = ("---\nid: user-auth\nname: User Auth\n"
               "version: 1.0.0\nauthor: MAM Team\nruntime: python\n---")
    data = extract_metadata(content)
    assert data["id"] == "user-auth"
    assert validate_id("user-auth")
    assert validate_version("1.0.0")
    assert validate_runtime("python")
    assert validate_metadata(data) == []
    assert "Module Metadata" in document_metadata(data)
```

## Examples

### Valid Front Matter

```yaml
id: api-client
name: API Client
version: 1.1.0
author: MAM Team
runtime: python
tags:
  - client
  - http
```

### Invalid Ids

```text
User-Auth  invalid due to uppercase
123-starts  invalid because it starts with a digit
has--double  invalid because of consecutive hyphens
```

